LOCUS       pJL1-T7-TetO-GFP       2486 bp    DNA     circular SYN 12-OCT-2026
DEFINITION  TetR-repressed, aTc-inducible deGFP reporter with a C-terminal
            Strep-tag II. Sequence carried verbatim from the Google Doc
            "TetO-PLA in NB_CPRG" (named pJL1_T7-TetO-GFP there, 2026-10-12);
            coordinates located by string search and by translating the CDS.
ACCESSION   pJL1-T7-TetO-GFP
VERSION     pJL1-T7-TetO-GFP
KEYWORDS    .
SOURCE      .
  ORGANISM  .
            .
COMMENT     Built 2026-10-12 from the source Doc's inline sequence. The Doc
            gives no sequence-landmark table for this construct (unlike the
            Doc's own simple Promoter/operator/Coding sequence/Marker
            summary table); promoter, operator, RBS and CDS were located
            here by string search and confirmed by translating the CDS: 240
            aa, ending WSHPQFEK, the Strep-tag II sequence the Doc's own
            table states this construct carries. The KanR marker is not
            annotated, since the Doc gives no landmark for it.
